## Iteration 9 — the convergence pass over iteration 8 (2026-09-19)

**Scope:** the iteration-8 fix commit `6a69a23..7b56a09` (4 code files).
Engine: eight lenses + one Codex pass (clean, the third consecutive).
**Zero Blocking findings** — Security and Performance clean outright;
the actionable set is advisory polish, all fixed in the same commit as
this record:

**R12-56 — `declares_integration` was section-blind** (Correctness,
Wire/schema, Tests): an `integration = ["…"]` array under any other
table (e.g. `[package.metadata]`) would falsely mark a crate a
declarer. The detector now scopes to the `[features]` table; the
"array opener on the next line" variant raised alongside it is invalid
TOML (values must open on the key's line) and needs no arm — stated in
the doc comment. Negative case pinned.

**R12-57 — the sweep anchor could mis-blame** (Correctness,
Wire/schema): `find("--no-run")` captured the FIRST flag occurrence;
a comment naming the flag before the sweep would anchor on the comment
and fail with a misleading message (fail-closed, diagnostic-only).
`sweep_command` now skips `--no-run` occurrences whose command carries
no `/integration` feature — a decoy comment before the workspace test
is pinned to stay green.

**R12-58 — the rejected-batch test could pass vacuously under double
drift** (Correctness): nothing proved the reader's search machinery was
live before asserting the other-project row stays hidden. The reader
now writes its own valid grant-proj control row first and must see it
before the negative phase. Mutation re-proven on the hardened test
(weakened guard → red, restored → green).

**R12-59 — `read_json_id`'s skip branch was unpinned** (Tests) and
comment volume (Cleanup): a unit test feeds an unrelated-id line then
the wanted one and asserts the right one returns; the sweep_command doc
and test glosses cut; the thrice-pasted per-binary-allow rationale is
one module-level note.

**Recorded, not fixed:** `read_json_id` is the module's first
single-consumer pub item (defensible as `read_json`'s id-matched
sibling; note in the record); the three poll loops' shared spine judged
load-bearing (their exit contracts differ); iteration 9's lenses
re-verified the accepted>0 semantics against every server ack path
(whole-batch atomic, replay returns the settled count — no
partial-commit-with-zero case exists).

**Retired:** the rust-analyzer E0107 reports (stale index — the tree
compiles and tests green); the server partial-acceptance question
(traced: whole-batch atomic at `service.rs:1607`, replay carries the
settled count at `:2051`); my own prompt's publish=false premise
(corrected by a lens: three of the six sweep targets are publish=false,
and the bijection is publish-agnostic by design). **Carried unverified,
unchanged:** the six live-gated/analyzer questions plus the PLT1
principal-membership question.

## Iteration 10 — the second convergence pass (2026-09-20)

